    "summary": "Epic Dark Star marathon, soaring Here Comes Sunshine, tight jams",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a monster 43‑minute Dark Star that segues into Eyes of the World and Stella Blue, plus an incandescent Here Comes Sunshine. Keith’s electric piano adds shimmering texture throughout, while Phil’s bass bombs drive the improvisations. Overall a high‑energy late‑’73 performance captured in excellent soundboard sources.",
    "review": "December 6, 1973 at Cleveland Public Auditorium finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. After a solid first set that includes the classic China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, the second set erupts with one of the era’s most celebrated Dark Stars – a soaring, space‑filled 43‑minute journey that rolls straight into an inspired Eyes of the World and a heartfelt Stella Blue. Here Comes Sunshine follows, its bright, uplifting vibe propelled by Jerry’s wailing lead tone and Keith’s jazzy electric piano. Phil’s bass bombs thunder through every jam, while Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart lock in with a propulsive groove that keeps the momentum relentless from start to finish. The Miller and Kaplan‑Fink‑Hamilton soundboards capture the band’s interplay with crystal‑clear separation, making this show a must‑listen for anyone chasing late‑’73 magic.",
